<title>POLAND: Cieszyn to omit 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>Cieszyn to omit 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>CIESZYN, Poland 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shareholders of Polish paintmaker Polifarb Cieszyn SA voted at an extraordinary meeting on Monday to omit a dividend for 1996.</p>
<p>The firm's president Bernard Andrzejewski said that of the 19.2 million zloty profit last year, 19.1 million would go to reserves and 107,000 zlotys as a bonus to the firm's supervisory board.</p>
<p>-- Wojciech Zurawski +48 22 653 9700</p>
